ter will have to give up  his marriage to mary jane  after consulting with mj parker accepts  thereby ruining his relationship with  his wife  and sacrificing their missing but  perhaps still alive daughter  who mephisto uses to taunt beta after he  makes his decision  putting aside the obvious fact that  faustian bargains rarely work out well  the one more dave's storyline makes it  very clear where spider-man's priorities  really lie it's obvious that peter  parker cares about army more than anyone  else  but that's not enough either he also  wants her all to himself  at least that's what it looks like  whenever mei starts to get close to a  man  other than peter spider-man interferes  and ruins everything  first off there's mae's husband ben  parker who dies after spider-man decides  he can't be bothered to stop a petty  crook  next in amazing spider-man issue 131  spider-man interrupts mae's wedding to  dark and leaves her groom to die in an  explosion on a crummy canadian island  her third serious boyfriend a gambler  named nathan lubinsky  passes away from a heart attack after  spider-man ruins his get-rich-quick  scheme  previously he had saved a casino owner  named raymond trask from assassination  at the hands of the vulture  thereby putting may and nathan in the  villains process and that's just the  beginning  when mei has a fling with edwin jarvis  the avengers butler  peter's deal with mephisto in one more  day wipes their relationship from  existence  in the recent clone conspiracy arc peter  refuses to let the mysterious medical  company  new you treat mae's third husband j  jonah jameson's father for a mysterious  disease  eventually peter changes his mind but by  then it's too late  and jay jameson is dead that's not a  great track record of course  and what's the common thread that  connects the end of each and every  relationship  why spider-man of course still may  manages to get a modicum of revenge  albeit unintentionally  when peter and dr oct